{{feat
|epic=yes
|type=general
|prereq=21st level, 20 [[skill rank|rank]]s in the chosen skill
|desc=The character gains a +10 bonus on all [[skill check]]s with the chosen [[skill]].
|use=automatic
|bonus1=assassin
|bonus2=bard
|bonus3=Harper scout
|bonus4=rogue
|bonus5=shadowdancer
}}

==Notes==
*Requires [[Hordes of the Underdark]].
*There is no ''epic skill focus'' in [[ride]].
*This feat [[stack]]s with [[skill focus]].
* ''Epic skill focus'' in a skill that is class-restricted (that does not allow [[cross-class skill|cross-class]] training) is also class-restricted, and the restrictions for the feat almost match those for the skill. ''Epic skill focus'' in [[animal empathy]] can be taken only when gaining a [[druid]], [[ranger]], or [[shifter]] level. ''Epic skill focus'' in [[perform]] can be taken only when gaining a [[bard]] level. ''Epic skill focus'' in [[use magic device]] can be taken only when gaining a [[bard]] or [[rogue]], or [[shadowdancer]] level (this would match the class restrictions on this skill if "shadowdancer" was replaced by "[[assassin]]").
* ''Epic skill focus'' in ''use magic device'' cannot be selected as a rogue [[bonus feat]], but otherwise bonus feat availability matches [[general feat]] availability.

==Custom content notes==
* The class restrictions on ''epic skill focus'' in ''animal empathy'', ''perform'', and ''use magic device'' are implemented by removing those variants from the general feat list and adding them to the feat lists for the allowed classes. Consequentially, a custom class must have those variants in its feat list in order for them to be available as [[general feat]]s.
